## Architectural Overview (Domain-Driven Design)

This Python microservice is built with **FastAPI** adhering to **Domain-Driven Design (DDD)** and **Hexagonal / Clean Architecture** principles:

```
[ Interfaces (REST API / Probes) ] ─────┐
                                        │
                                        ▼
                  [ Application Layer (Services / DTOs) ]
                                        │
                                        ▼
                   [ Domain Layer (Models / Exceptions / Repo Interface) ]
                                        ▲
                                        │
[ Infrastructure Layer (Async DB / HTTP Client) ] ──┘ (implements Domain Interfaces)
```

### Layer Structure

- **`app/main.py`**: FastAPI application factory, lifespan startup/shutdown hooks, global middlewares (CORS, Request ID, Exception Handlers).
- **`app/config.py`**: `pydantic-settings` BaseSettings configuration loaded from environment variables.
- **`app/domain/`**:
  - `models/`: Pure business models, Aggregate Roots, status enums, business validation rules.
  - `repositories/`: Abstract repository interfaces (`BaseRepository`) without framework dependencies.
  - `exceptions/`: Domain-specific business exceptions.
- **`app/application/`**:
  - `services/`: Use case orchestrator coordinating domain entities and infrastructure ports.
  - `dtos/`: Pydantic request and response schemas.
- **`app/infrastructure/`**:
  - `database/`: Async connection pooling and session management ({{.Database}}).
  - `repositories/`: Concrete async repository implementation stub.
  - `external/`: External service async HTTP client stub (`httpx`).
- **`app/interfaces/`**:
  - `api/router.py`: REST routes and path operations.
  - `api/dependencies.py`: FastAPI dependency injection.
- **`tests/`**:
  - `unit/`: Fast unit tests covering domain rules.
  - `integration/`: Async integration tests exercising HTTP endpoints.
- **`deploy/k8s/`**: Kubernetes deployment, service, and configmap manifests.

## Getting Started

### Prerequisites
- Python 3.12+
- Docker & Kubernetes (optional)

### Local Development
```bash
# Install dependencies in virtual environment
make install

# Run development server with live reload
make run

# Run test suite
make test

# Run linter
make lint
```

### Configuration
Configuration is loaded via environment variables or `.env` file:

| Variable | Description | Default |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `APP_ENV` | Environment (`development`, `staging`, `production`) | `development` |
| `PORT` | HTTP listen port | `{{.Port}}` |
| `DATABASE_URL` | Database connection URL | `{{.Database}}://...` |
| `LOG_LEVEL` | Logging level (`DEBUG`, `INFO`, `WARNING`, `ERROR`) | `INFO` |
| `LOG_FORMAT` | Log format (`json`, `text`) | `json` |

## API Endpoints

- `GET /healthz` - Kubernetes liveness probe
- `GET /readyz` - Kubernetes readiness probe
- `GET /docs` - OpenAPI Swagger UI
- `POST /api/v1/entities` - Create entity
- `GET /api/v1/entities/{id}` - Retrieve entity
- `PUT /api/v1/entities/{id}` - Update entity
- `DELETE /api/v1/entities/{id}` - Delete entity
- `GET /api/v1/entities` - List entities (supports `?offset=0&limit=20`)
- `POST /api/v1/entities/{id}/activate` - Activate entity
